From: Connor Baker <ConnorBaker01@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hydra-eval-jobset: make nix-eval-jobs' --max-jobs configurable

`hydra-eval-jobset` always passed `--max-jobs 1`, and the daemon applies a
client's `max-jobs` to the builds it runs locally for that connection. So an
evaluation that imports from derivations builds them one at a time, however
many it asks for at once.

Read it from `evaluator_max_jobs` in hydra.conf instead, defaulting to 1 as
before. This is the setting NixOS/hydra#2040 (commit 54b37ab4) adds to the
Rust evaluator, under the same name, in evaluator.toml.
---
--- a/script/hydra-eval-jobset
+++ b/script/hydra-eval-jobset
@@ -423,7 +423,7 @@ sub evalJobsCmd {
     }
 
     push @cmd, ("--gc-roots-dir", $gcRootsDir) if defined $gcRootsDir;
-    push @cmd, ("--max-jobs", 1);
+    push @cmd, ("--max-jobs", $config->{evaluator_max_jobs} // 1);
     push @cmd, "--meta";
     push @cmd, "--constituents";
     push @cmd, "--force-recurse";
